3]Explain indetail about inner class in java ?

	->In java an inner class is a class that is declared inside another class is called as inner class in java.
	->Inner classes where mainly introduced to group the logically related classes together making the code
	more readable and maintainable
	->Java supports 4 types of inner class:-
		i)Nested non static inner class
		ii)Nested static inner class
		iii)Local Class
		iv)Anonymous inner class
		

Nested non static inner class:-
===============================
	->Nested non static inner class dont have any static keyword
	
	Properties:
		i)It requires the instance of the outer class to be created
		ii)It can access all the members of outer class including the private one's
		

Nested static inner class:-
============================
	->Nested static inner class is declared using static keyword
	
	Properties:
		i)It does not requires the instance of the outer class
		ii)It can access the static members of the outer class
		iii)It cannot access the non static members of the outer class

Local class:-
=============
	
	->Local class in java are classes which are defined with in a block of code such as with in a method,constructor
	or intializer block
	->Local classes are similar to inner classes but they are local to the block of code in which they are
	defined
	->Local class can access the variables and parameters of the enclosing block
	
	
Anonymous inner class:-
=======================
	
	->Anonymous inner class is a type of inner class in java they dont have any name
	->They are typically used for one time use,often declared within the body of another class or method
	
	
1]Can we have more than one class in java file ?

	->Yes,we can have more than one class in a java file
	

2]Can we have more than one public class in a java file ?
	
	->No,we cannot have more than one public class in a java file

	
3]How many class files will be generated when multiple classes are present in a java file ? 

	->Multiple class files will be generated when multiple classes are present in a java file
	

4]Can we have main method in all the classes present at root level of java file ?

	->Yes,we can have main method in all the classes present at root level of java file,but while execution
	it will ask us to select which class to execute or run
	

5]If a java file contains more than one class at the root level are they considers as inner classes ?

	->No
	
6]Can we have more than one inner class in a given class ?

	->Yes,we can have more than one inner class in a given class
	

7]Can we create a public/private/protected inner class ?
	
	->Yes,we can create public/private/protected inner class
	
	
8]Can we create a static/abstract/final inner class ?
	
	->Yes,we can create static/abstract/final inner class
	

9]Can we create a main method inside the inner class ?

	->Yes,in static inner class we can create main method.
	->we cannot create main method in non static inner class
	
	
10]How to access the outer class variables when they are duplicated in inner class ?

	->Local variables are accessed directly
	->To access the instance variable of inner class we use this,and variable name
	->To access the instance variable of outer class we use className,this and variable name
	
11]Can an inner class extend any non-abstract class ?

	->Yes,an inner class can extend any non-abstract class.
	
	
12]Can an inner class extend an abstract class ?
	
		->Yes,an inner class can extend an abstract class.
		

13]Can an inner class implement any interface ?

	->Yes,an inner class can implement any interface
	
	
14]Can we call inner classes outside the outer class

	->Yes,we can call the inner classes outside the outer class
